# 8th Grade ELA

Ms. Patel is planning an argument writing unit where students will develop and defend a claim using evidence. She knows that AI can quickly generate entire arguments, which could undermine the learning goal if students rely on it too heavily. However, she also sees value in using AI to expose students to different perspectives and strengthen their reasoning.

She decides to structure this as an AI-assisted assignment, where AI supports idea development but students remain fully responsible for their argument.

To establish clear boundaries, Ms. Patel allows students to use AI for brainstorming claims, generating counterarguments, or getting feedback on clarity. However, students are not allowed to submit AI-written paragraphs. More importantly, they are expected to evaluate any AI-generated ideas and decide whether to use them.

As she designs the assignment, Ms. Patel builds in multiple checkpoints to make student thinking visible. Students begin by developing their own claim and outline without AI. This ensures they have an initial position before encountering outside input.

Next, students use AI to generate a counterargument to their claim. Rather than simply accepting it, they must analyze it: Is it strong? Is it supported? Does it change their thinking? Ms. Patel includes a structured response where students either incorporate the counterargument into their essay or explain why they rejected it.

During drafting, students annotate their work to show where AI influenced their thinking. For example, they might note, “AI suggested this counterargument, but I revised it to include stronger evidence,” or “I chose not to use this idea because it lacked support.”

She also includes a short reflection at the end of the assignment, asking students to explain how AI helped or did not help their thinking.

When grading, Ms. Patel prioritizes reasoning, evidence, and decision-making. She looks at the strength of the argument, but also at how students engaged with AI. A student who thoughtfully critiques an AI suggestion demonstrates deeper understanding than one who passively includes it.
MARKDOWN
